The '''Resistance base''', also known as the '''D'Qar base''', '''Resistance headquarters''', or as '''Saw Gerrera's base''', was the base operated by the [[Resistance]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[planet]] [[D'Qar]], during their [[Cold War|conflict]] with the [[First Order]]. After the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destruction]] of the [[Hosnian system]], the base was used to plan the [[Battle of Starkiller Base|assault]] on [[Starkiller Base]], the First Order's planet-converted [[superweapon]]. However, it was soon destroyed by First Order forces during the [[Battle of D'Qar]].

==Description==
[[File:Resistance_HQ_SWDA.png|thumb|left|250px|The Resistance base command center]]
The [[Resistance]] base,<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> or Saw Gerrera's base<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=news/andor-trivia-guide-week-2|text=Secrets from the Set of ''Andor'' Season 2: Week 2 Trivia}}</ref> when it was used by [[Saw Gerrera]]'s [[Partisans]] during the [[Imperial Era]],<ref name="Ever Been">{{Andor|Ever Been to Ghorman?}}</ref> was located mostly underneath the surface of [[D'Qar]], with only the facility's landing areas and antenna arrays exposed. Inside the base was a command center, as well as as multiple [[hangar]]s, both above and underground, used to store [[T-70 X-wing starfighter]]s. Underneath the hangars was an area known as the maintenance level, where damaged vehicles could go to be repaired. Surrounding the base was thick [[Tree|jungle]] foliage, which helped hide the facility from air and ground [[sensor]]s and conceal potential power leaks. Most of the equipment used at the base was portable, a feature insisted by [[General]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] due to her experience of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance's]] [[Battle of Hoth|near-extinction]] on [[Hoth]].<ref name="CL" />

==History==
In [[3 BBY]], [[Saw Gerrera]] and his [[Partisans]] operated out of the base. After discovering the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[spy]] [[Pluti]] among their ranks, they left the base on D'Qar behind.<ref name="FriendsEverywhere">{{Andor|I Have Friends Everywhere}}</ref> After being scouted by [[Corona Squadron]]<ref name="TFA VD">''[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> sometime after the [[Battle of Hoth]],<ref name="Lost Stars">''[[Lost Stars]]''</ref> the location was then considered for usage by the formal [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] as a possible base.<ref name="TFA VD" /> Only ever serving a small outpost for the Alliance,<ref name="CLNew">''[[Star Wars: Complete Locations, New Edition]]''</ref> however, the base was used towards the end of the [[Galactic Civil War]] but was abandoned shortly after its establishment to focus on pursuing the retreating [[Imperial Military]].<ref name="TFA VD" />

When [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] was revealed to be [[Senator]] Leia Organa's biological [[Parent|father]] twenty-four [[Standard year|years]] after the formation of the [[New Republic]], Organa's reputation was impacted dramatically.<ref name="Bloodline">[[Bloodline (novel)|''Bloodline'']]</ref> Believing there to be a new threat facing [[the galaxy]], Organa pleaded with the Republic to investigate, however, her protests about the [[Military Disarmament Act]] were dismissed as paranoia, while her warnings of the growing [[First Order]] were misconstrued as warmongering. Having no other option, she formed the Resistance to combat the threat of full-scale war once again engulfing the galaxy.<ref name="CL" />

In need of a base of operations, Organa remembered D'Qar's abandoned Rebel Alliance outpost and sent [[engineer]]s to expand the facility.<ref name="CLNew" /> The base was the launch point of several missions and offensives against the First Order.<ref name="TFA VD" /> In the [[34 ABY|thirtieth year]] after the [[Battle of Endor]], the Resistance received word that the [[astromech droid]], [[BB-8]], who was in possession of a map leading to [[Jedi]] [[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Luke Skywalker]], was on the [[Mid Rim Territories|Mid Rim]] planet, [[Takodana]].<ref name="TFA">{{Film|VII}}</ref>

Within minutes, the First Order, having also received the same information, arrived at the planet and attacked [[Takodana Castle|the castle]] BB-8 was located at. Shortly after, however, [[Resistance Starfighter Corps|Resistance pilots]] also arrived, and [[Battle of Takodana|engaged]] the First Order's [[First Order Navy|air]] and [[First Order Army|ground forces]]. During the battle, the First Order captured the [[scavenger]], [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] and retreated, believing they had got what they came for. After arriving back at the Resistance base, [[Finn]], a deserter [[First Order stormtrooper]], gave the Resistance intel on how to destroy [[Starkiller Base]], the First Order's planet-converted [[superweapon]], which had recently [[Hosnian Cataclysm|destroyed]] the Rebublic's [[capital]], [[Hosnian Prime]], and was now targeting D'Qar. After identifying Starkiller Base's weak point as its [[thermal oscillator]], the Resistance starfighter pilots began preparing their ships for battle, while Finn, [[Han Solo]], and [[Chewbacca]] readied Solo's ship, the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]''. [[Battle of Starkiller Base|Arriving]] at Starkiller Base, Finn, Solo, and Chewbacca managed to lower Starkiller's shields, rescue Rey, and blow an opening in its thermal oscillator, allowing [[Poe Dameron]], leader of the Resistance starfighter corps, to enter and destroy it. With the superweapon destroyed, D'Qar and the Resistance base was safe from destruction.<ref name="TFA" />

Arriving back at base, [[R2-D2]], who had been in low-power mode since Skywalker's disappearance, overheard Rey stating that the First Order had recovered the majority of the starchart that was recovered from the [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] archives, but they were still lacking the final piece to match with the fragment BB-8 had acquired. The [[droid]] promptly reactivated after years of hibernation, and searched his records and found that he had previously downloaded this map while upon the first [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]].<ref name="TFA novel" /> Projecting the map into the room, R2-D2 matched his map with the piece that BB-8 held, revealing [[Ahch-To|the location]] of the [[first Jedi Temple]], and in turn, Luke Skywalker. With this revelation, R2-D2, Rey, and Chewbacca left the base in the ''Millennium Falcon'' in search of the Jedi Master.<ref name="TFA" />

Shortly after, anticipating an attack by the First Order, the Resistance personnel scrambled frantically to transfer personnel and equipment to the flagship [[Raddus (MC85 Star Cruiser)|''Raddus'']] in orbit. Led by Lieutenant [[Kaydel Ko Connix]], they managed to completely clear the base and [[Battle of D'Qar|evacuate]] mere seconds before it was fired on and destroyed by the [[Mandator IV-class Siege Dreadnought|''Mandator IV''-class Siege Dreadnought]] ''[[Fulminatrix]]''.<ref name="Episode VIII" />

==Personnel==
[[File:Blue_Squadron_Pilot_2016_X-Wing_Open_alt_card.png|thumb|right|250px|Three X-wings of Blue Squadron]]
The upper levels of the [[Resistance High Command|Resistance hierarchy]] consisted mainly of veterans of the [[Galactic Civil War]] who had served alongside Leia Organa in the Rebel Alliance. High ranking individuals included General [[Cypress]], a commander of the Resistance [[Resistance Army|ground forces]], [[Major]] [[Taslin Brance]], a [[communications officer]] who kept Organa up-to-date on First Order operations, Major [[Caluan Ematt]], a well-traveled veteran of the Galactic Civil War, [[Admiral]] [[Ushos O. Statura|Statura]], who fought against the Empire during the [[Liberation of Garel|liberation]] of his home planet of [[Garel]], and Admiral [[Gial Ackbar]], an experienced commander who fought in the [[Clone Wars]] and was instrumental to the Rebel Alliance's victory over the Galactic Empire.<ref name="TFA VD" />

Poe Dameron was the leader of [[Black Squadron (Resistance)|Black Squadron]],<ref name="PD1">[[Poe Dameron 1|''Poe Dameron'' 1]]</ref> [[Red Squadron (Resistance)|Red Squadron]], and [[Blue Squadron (Resistance)|Blue Squadron]] under the [[callsign]] [[Black Leader]].<ref name="TFA VD" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Resistance base first appeared in the Junior novels ''[[The Weapon of a Jedi: A Luke Skywalker Adventure]]'' and ''[[Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure]]'', two books that were part of the ''[[Journey to Star Wars: The Force Awakens]]'', a multimedia project of a series of at least twenty books and comics that featured content related to the film leading up to the [[2015]] ''[[Star Wars]]'' film, [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']]. The scene show was taken at RAF Greenham Common, A Former Royal Air Force station.

